e complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-40+30\\text{i}}{25}=-\\frac{40}{25}+\\frac{30}{25}\\text{i}=-\\frac{8}{5}+\\frac{6}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74649/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74649"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316872/field-1/0e0b7f0c6ddc9443ebb52e486a1859bbf690930fb1e7c57cc7012d23ebdf96a7" :answer/id #uuid "43b52200-9269-5ea7-beb6-272c1721daae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316872/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f4fa94e-0332-59f4-8a4d-3dd24e907dae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316872/field-1/0e0b7f0c6ddc9443ebb52e486a1859bbf690930fb1e7c57cc7012d23ebdf96a7" :answer-field/choices ["q-316872/field-1/0e0b7f0c6ddc9443ebb52e486a1859bbf690930fb1e7c57cc7012d23ebdf96a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316872/field-2/4beac40be125df285f94d814b05265c6d87392bc3fc5802cfcf75e96a47b31b3" :answer/id #uuid "2169ea74-a372-5c4b-8838-f967e2b52338" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316872/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f994d418-900c-5adb-a627-171c2efb5cf7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316872/field-2/4beac40be125df285f94d814b05265c6d87392bc3fc5802cfcf75e96a47b31b3" :answer-field/choices ["q-316872/field-2/4beac40be125df285f94d814b05265c6d87392bc3fc5802cfcf75e96a47b31b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316872" :question/id #uuid "d5915603-e652-5ba7-a613-b88aecd96c3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-316872" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{5}{-2+3\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-2+3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2-3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{-2+3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5}{-2+3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2-3\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(-2-3\\text{i})}{(-2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-15\\text{i}}{4-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-15\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{-10-15\\text{i}}{13}=(-\\frac{10}{13})+(-\\frac{15}{13})\\,\\text{i}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316872/field-1" "q-316872/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316872"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316891/field-1/8a8bea9daeb7245298b0ee172ce0c458b3aae0c200f414e473745de2fe88c4ab" :answer/id #uuid "6def0763-0118-5b51-9c8d-aab0ebc7a1f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316891/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e13f8ccf-eab4-57e7-b21f-5c959ecb417c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316891/field-1/8a8bea9daeb7245298b0ee172ce0c458b3aae0c200f414e473745de2fe88c4ab" :answer-field/choices ["q-316891/field-1/8a8bea9daeb7245298b0ee172ce0c458b3aae0c200f414e473745de2fe88c4ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316891/field-2/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "90ec2cd9-0932-58d4-9c41-4ca9408e9a70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316891/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "27657b89-78a5-5728-a415-4e0c075ac551" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316891/field-2/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-316891/field-2/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316891" :question/id #uuid "0d55d864-b6fe-5c73-b70e-93372f20943b" :question/math-academy-id "q-316891" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{-5-9\\text{i}}{10\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $10\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+10\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-10\\text{i},$ or simply $-10\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-10\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-5-9\\text{i}}{10\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-5-9\\text{i}}{10\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-10\\text{i}}{-10\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{50\\text{i}+90{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-100{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{50\\text{i}+90(-1)}{-100(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-90+50\\text{i}}{100}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-90+50\\text{i}}{100} & =-\\frac{90}{100}+\\frac{50}{100}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{9}{10})+(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316891/field-1" "q-316891/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316891"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-167676/selection/11d16509fd97a074c04641535c291a4d84a46c2f06dadf4d29b15eaae9c249c9" :answer/id #uuid "084a5f6e-3881-53f1-90f5-6a65a168ce55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167676/selection/9428d975924a779ea322162c8d95b9ecce9b00a118925b5d054c460d6bf7b37c" :answer/id #uuid "57c1c406-2e15-5e3d-8750-9315e5f8f88d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{2}{9}i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167676/selection/da3ca95a265204cad321c21bafb580815bc385dc48402cbae69a989a8a7a2196" :answer/id #uuid "d53d6f75-887d-547c-86ca-d8eb886b12bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167676/selection/c9f95b4f476e55caf4dc068f3609aa6480cd0712b6c762095cc03eaefc8ad275" :answer/id #uuid "a4966510-e88a-5700-87ed-663bb022eb83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}-2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167676/selection/59962de45076bbe81d0c7f713da089d5dea0fbef6b17b7e1985d61b283b74a5c" :answer/id #uuid "57d41e20-d8fe-5176-a520-922edf91372f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}+2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167676/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0d9bd20-96ee-5744-b296-f53a156df837" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-167676/selection/c9f95b4f476e55caf4dc068f3609aa6480cd0712b6c762095cc03eaefc8ad275" :answer-field/choices ["q-167676/selection/11d16509fd97a074c04641535c291a4d84a46c2f06dadf4d29b15eaae9c249c9" "q-167676/selection/9428d975924a779ea322162c8d95b9ecce9b00a118925b5d054c460d6bf7b37c" "q-167676/selection/da3ca95a265204cad321c21bafb580815bc385dc48402cbae69a989a8a7a2196" "q-167676/selection/c9f95b4f476e55caf4dc068f3609aa6480cd0712b6c762095cc03eaefc8ad275" "q-167676/selection/59962de45076bbe81d0c7f713da089d5dea0fbef6b17b7e1985d61b283b74a5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-167676" :question/id #uuid "4f7f340b-160f-5ff4-a53d-52f410581d8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-167676" :question/problem "$\\frac{6-4\\text{i}}{3\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $3\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+3\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-3\\text{i},$ or simply $-3\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6-4\\text{i}}{3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{6-4\\text{i}}{3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-3\\text{i}}{-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18\\text{i}+12{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-9{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18\\text{i}+12(-1)}{-9(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-12-18\\text{i}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-12-18\\text{i}}{9} & =-\\frac{12}{9}-\\frac{18}{9}\\text{i} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-167676/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-167676"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316886/field-1/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" :answer/id #uuid "1e2a34c0-1ac1-5140-a670-d310b4a3ba4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316886/field-1/b01ba7e917b2f2dc3ff90ccb2c435764c9ebef2dea263cc318e0c231eb7eeb1d" :answer/id #uuid "bb4bc66f-5ae0-5f58-a1e6-a9582186c253" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316886/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3ebef65-aece-5350-a453-99badfd1fe77" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316886/field-1/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" :answer-field/choices ["q-316886/field-1/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" "q-316886/field-1/b01ba7e917b2f2dc3ff90ccb2c435764c9ebef2dea263cc318e0c231eb7eeb1d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316886/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "42066600-9df5-5a91-808a-1517bd3923ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316886/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8c0b29c-a4c9-579a-a525-4e18cab1c0ba" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316886/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-316886/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316886" :question/id #uuid "62c0981c-dc22-5dd8-9db1-93ade390bfe9" :question/math-academy-id "q-316886" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{-12+5\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $4\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+4\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-4\\text{i},$ or simply $-4\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-12+5\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-12+5\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-4\\text{i}}{-4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{48\\text{i}-20{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{48\\text{i}-20(-1)}{-16(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{20+48\\text{i}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{20+48\\text{i}}{16} & =\\frac{20}{16}+\\frac{48}{16}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{4})+(3)\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316886/field-1" "q-316886/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316886"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316888/field-1/b8fe8d3cb42910de21f3df8634e1c373223a74d32bfef959cca9ceacd5c4d03e" :answer/id #uuid "477fbecb-e5a4-5569-8eea-8ce894cd68c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316888/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "29008319-9cf4-50b5-b3b0-892033bd0dfe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316888/field-1/b8fe8d3cb42910de21f3df8634e1c373223a74d32bfef959cca9ceacd5c4d03e" :answer-field/choices ["q-316888/field-1/b8fe8d3cb42910de21f3df8634e1c373223a74d32bfef959cca9ceacd5c4d03e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316888/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "272244b3-8eba-577b-b934-35edb47685b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316888/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5842e02f-2e2b-567d-981f-2d4c60c02eaf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316888/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-316888/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316888" :question/id #uuid "77aba267-0ace-52cd-b48c-fb373812d066" :question/math-academy-id "q-316888" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{-6-7\\text{i}}{2\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $2\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+2\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-2\\text{i},$ or simply $-2\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-6-7\\text{i}}{2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-6-7\\text{i}}{2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2\\text{i}}{-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\text{i}+14{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\text{i}+14(-1)}{-4(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14+12\\text{i}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-14+12\\text{i}}{4} & =-\\frac{14}{4}+\\frac{12}{4}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{7}{2})+(3)\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316888/field-1" "q-316888/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316888"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5780"] :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}}$ in the form $a+\\textrm{i}b.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $1-\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $1+\\textrm{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1+\\textrm{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}} \n&=\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {1 + \\textrm{i}} {1 + \\textrm{i}}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {4 + 4\\textrm{i} + \\textrm{i} + \\textrm{i}^2} {1^2 - \\textrm{i}^2}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {4 + 5\\textrm{i} + (-1)} {1 - (-1)}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {3 + 5\\textrm{i}} {2}\t\n\t}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+\\textrm{i} b \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {3 + 5\\textrm{i}} {2} =\n\t\t\\dfrac{3} {2} + \\dfrac {5} {2} \\textrm{i}\t\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6230"] :question/problem "If $z_1=3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2 = 2+5\\textrm{i},$ then what is $z_1$ divided by $z_2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3\\textrm{i}}{2+5\\textrm i}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is $2+5\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $2-5\\textrm{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $2-5\\textrm{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {3 \\textrm{i}} {2 +5\\textrm{i}} \n&= \\dfrac {3 \\textrm{i}} {2 +5 \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {2 -5 \\textrm{i}} {2-5\\textrm{i}}  \\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15 \\textrm{i}^2 } {2^2 - (5\\textrm{i})^2}  \\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15\\textrm{i}^2 } {4 - 25\\textrm{i}^2} \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15(-1) } {4 - 25(-1)}  \\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} + 15 } {29}\n\t}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} + 15 } {29}=\n\t\t\\dfrac{15} {29} + \\dfrac {6} {29} \\textrm{i}\t\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6231"] :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac{4}{-1+2\\textrm{i} }$ in the form $a+\\textrm{i}b.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-1+2\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $-1-2\\textrm{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-1-2\\textrm{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {4} {-1 +2\\textrm{i}} \n&=\\dfrac {4} {-1 +2 \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {-1 -2 \\textrm{i}} {-1-2\\textrm{i}}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {(-1)^2 - (2\\textrm{i})^2}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {1 - 4\\textrm{i}^2}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {1 - 4(-1)}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {5} \n\t}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {5} =\n\t\t-\\dfrac{4} {5} - \\dfrac {8} {5} \\textrm{i}\t\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5781"] :question/problem "If $z_1 = -8-3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2 = 2\\textrm{i},$ then what is $z_1$ divided by $z_2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is the imaginary number $2\\textrm{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+2\\textrm{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-2\\textrm{i},$ or simply $-2\\textrm{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2\\textrm{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}} \n&= \t\\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {-2\\textrm{i}} {-2\\textrm{i}} \\[5pt]\n&= \t\\dfrac {16\\textrm{i} + 6\\textrm{i}^2} {-4\\textrm{i}^2} \\[5pt]\n&= \t\\dfrac {16\\textrm{i} + 6(-1)} {-4(-1)} \\[5pt]\n&= \t\\dfrac {-6 + 16\\textrm{i}} {4}\t\t\t\n\t}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {-6 + 16\\textrm{i}} {4} &= - \\dfrac{6}{4} + \\dfrac{16}{4} \\textrm{i} \\[5pt]\n&=\t\t-\\dfrac{3} {2} + 4\\textrm{i}\t\t\t\t\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
